{:id "0016-look-title-sequence"
 :title "The look: messages set like title cards, Scout's presence as a Bit"
 :lupa/deps #{"0006-views" "0013-e2e-smoke"}
 :lupa/area :ui
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "Half Ahead gets its first visual identity (DECISIONS.md H15): paper
        and ink, messages set like title cards rather than boxed chat
        bubbles, reading first, and Scout's presence shown as a small
        Bit-like glyph whose shape is its state. Along the way, fix four
        things the first screenshot and audit showed: the author line runs
        name and owner together (\"Scoutagent of Ben\"), the reduced-motion
        checkbox does nothing when clicked, a performance can only be
        skipped with a mouse, and every message shows a replay button."
 :scope ["public/css/halfahead.css" "src/halfahead/app/views.cljc"
         "test/halfahead/app/views_test.cljc"]
 :design "Read docs/research/conversation-design.md first (principles and
          direction 2, \"title sequence\").

          CSS (tokens only on :root; light 'paper' and dark 'ink' schemes
          via prefers-color-scheme):
          - Paper: warm off-white background, warm near-black ink, one
            signal colour (a vermilion) used sparingly for the agent's
            glyph and focus rings. Dark: the inverse, warm, never pure
            black or white. Body text contrast at least 7:1 (WCAG AAA) in
            both schemes; state the pairs in a comment.
          - Type: messages in a readable serif stack (ui-serif, Georgia,
            serif) at a comfortable size (1.125rem+), measure about 60-70ch;
            author lines and the conversation title in a condensed sans
            stack, small caps or letter-spaced uppercase, like credits. No
            web-font downloads.
          - Messages are not boxed: generous vertical space and a hairline
            rule between turns; agent turns indented a little with the
            glyph in the margin.
          - Effects keep their meaning: .fx-slam scales from large (the
            game-show card, used rarely) and settles; .fx-rise lifts like a
            credit line; .fx-whisper is smaller and quieter; reduced motion
            shows everything still.
          - The replay button is visible on hover and on keyboard focus
            within the message, hidden otherwise (but always reachable by
            Tab).

          Views (halfahead.app.views, pure; keep all existing behaviour):
          - Author line: the name, then a visually separated owner line
            for agents (e.g. a middle dot and smaller type); the text
            content must read \"Scout · agent of Ben\" (with spaces).
          - Presence glyph: an inline SVG for each agent member, shown with
            the presence line and beside the agent's messages, with
            data-state \"idle\" or \"thinking\" and three simple shapes (a
            diamond for idle, a star-like stellated shape for thinking).
            aria-hidden; the presence line text remains the accessible
            signal. Under reduced motion the glyph does not animate.
          - Skip: while a message is performing it shows a real <button>
            \"Skip\" (keyboard reachable) emitting [[:message/skipped {:id
            id}]]; the article no longer needs a click handler.
          - Preferences: each checkbox emits its toggled value,
            [[:prefs/changed {:reduced-motion? (not current)}]] and
            [[:prefs/changed {:sound? (not current)}]]."
 :acceptance
 ["View tests: the agent's author line text is \"Scout · agent of Ben\" (a
   separator with spaces between name and owner line)"
  "View tests: a performing message has a <button> with text \"Skip\" whose
   click event is [[:message/skipped {:id id}]]; a settled message has none"
  "View tests: the reduced-motion checkbox's change event carries the
   negation of the current preference (both directions), and the sound
   checkbox's likewise"
  "View tests: each agent member has a glyph with data-state equal to its
   presence state (default \"idle\"); glyphs are aria-hidden"
  "All existing view tests still pass (sr-only copy, segments concatenate to
   the text, presence line, composer)"
  "CSS: tokens only on :root for colours; a light and a dark scheme; a
   prefers-reduced-motion block; the contrast pairs listed in a comment"
  "`bb e2e` still passes, and the final message lists the new screenshot
   paths (out/e2e/*.png) for the foreman to look at"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit core, perform, the shell, the schema, or the worker"
  "No credit roll, sound, or new deliveries yet; no web fonts or images"]
 :context ["docs/research/conversation-design.md" "DESIGN.md" "PRODUCT.md"
           "src/halfahead/app/views.cljc" "public/css/halfahead.css"
           "test/halfahead/app/views_test.cljc" "src/halfahead/app/core.cljc"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
